  "rationale": "All 20 candidates are direct matches on trait_reported/trait_efo (basal cell carcinoma). Most models come from the Cancer PRSweb family (PGS000445–PGS000459) with similar phenotype and covariates (age/sex/batch/PCs 1–4) and AUROC values mostly ~0.52–0.63. PGS000119 (PRSWeb, PLoS Genet) has clean endpoint alignment (phenotyping_reported: Basal cell carcinoma) and basic covariates, and shows the strongest reported discrimination among the provided candidates (AUROC=0.64, 95% CI 0.62–0.66) with a supportive per-SD OR=1.65 (1.56–1.75). The main limitation is that the reported AUROC appears to be a full-model AUROC (not explicitly PRS-only), and some Cancer PRSweb siblings have higher Nagelkerke R² and top-1% ORs (e.g., PGS000452/PGS000454), making the margin less decisive; however, those alternatives do not exceed PGS000119 on AUROC in the visible evidence."
}

